   "hypothesis_id": "H1",
   "mechanism": "Excess MUC5B in the distal airway thickens the mucus gel and slows clearance, so inhaled and microbial insults persist at the bronchioalveolar junction. Reduced TOLLIP removes the brake on TLR and TGF-beta signalling, so each retained insult produces a larger and longer profibrotic response. The two act on the same lesion from opposite ends: one raises the exposure, the other raises the gain.",
