   "hypothesis_id": "H2",
   "mechanism": "Alveolar type II cells are the progenitor pool for alveolar repair. Short telomeres from TERT haploinsufficiency cap how many times that pool can divide; misfolded SFTPC proprotein loads the same cells with ER stress. Both routes end in senescence or apoptosis of the identical cell type, which is why unrelated genes give the same histology: the alveolus cannot re-epithelialise after injury, and fibroblasts fill the space instead.",
